CRASH-10: range-check the node indexes read from a binary RDII file

readRdiiFileHeader() used each node index stored in a binary RDII interface
file to read Node[j] without checking that j is a node of the current model.
A file written by another model, or before nodes were added or deleted,
reads outside the Node array (heap overflow or segmentation fault). An index
outside 0..Nobjects[NODE]-1 is now ERROR 345, like an index of a node that
has no RDII inflow.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CRASH-10_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c b/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
index d8835c5..bd276b9 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/rdii.c
@@ -621,6 +621,7 @@ int readRdiiFileHeader()
     for ( i=0; i<NumRdiiNodes; i++ )
     {
         j = RdiiNodeIndex[i];
+        if ( j < 0 || j >= Nobjects[NODE] ) return ERR_RDII_FILE_FORMAT;
         if ( Node[j].rdiiInflow == NULL ) return ERR_RDII_FILE_FORMAT;
     }
     if ( feof(Frdii.file) ) return ERR_RDII_FILE_FORMAT;
